Cause : la liste « Company skill library » ne montrait que la clé de
bibliothèque (company/<id>/routage-coordination). Les agents appelaient
Skill avec cette clé et Claude Code répondait « Unknown skill » : 12 appels
sur 12 en échec dans l'usine (mesure du 27/10/2026), donc aucun skill
d'entreprise jamais chargé. Claude Code 2.1.308 ne connaît que le nom du
dossier monté (routage-coordination--32f74c7bdc), prouvé par trois appels
forcés (nom de dossier : chargé ; clé : Unknown skill).

Correctif : pour un skill activé, la ligne donne son runtimeName et dit de
ne jamais charger par la clé. Les skills non activés n'exposent pas leur
nom d'exécution. Échecs de la suite adapter-utils identiques avant et après
(175, bac à sable, git, ACP), sauf le nouveau test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012hDEUaJZ3u1rGj4CzNXrhC
---
 .../src/skill-library-manifest.test.ts         | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../src/skill-library-manifest.ts              |  5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/adapter-utils/src/skill-library-manifest.test.ts b/packages/adapter-utils/src/skill-library-manifest.test.ts
index 34a86591a..3935a034a 100644
--- a/packages/adapter-utils/src/skill-library-manifest.test.ts
+++ b/packages/adapter-utils/src/skill-library-manifest.test.ts
@@ -55,6 +55,24 @@ describe("buildSkillLibraryManifestMarkdown", () => {
     expect(shuffled).toBe(manifest);
   });
 
+  it("names the runtime skill to load for enabled skills, since the runtime does not know the library key", () => {
+    // Atelier, 27/10/2026: agents called Skill with the library key ("company/<id>/routage-coordination")
+    // and Claude Code answered "Unknown skill" 12 times out of 12; the mounted name works.
+    const manifest = buildSkillLibraryManifestMarkdown({
+      entries: [
+        entry({ key: "company/c1/routage-coordination", runtimeName: "routage-coordination--32f74c7bdc" }),
+        entry({ key: "company/c1/audit-seo", runtimeName: "audit-seo--8379c5d388" }),
+      ],
+      desiredSkillKeys: new Set(["company/c1/routage-coordination"]),
+    });
+
+    expect(manifest).toContain(
+      "- company/c1/routage-coordination — enabled; load it by its runtime name `routage-coordination--32f74c7bdc`, never by this key",
+    );
+    expect(manifest).toContain("- company/c1/audit-seo — installed, not enabled for you");
+    expect(manifest).not.toContain("audit-seo--8379c5d388");
+  });
+
   it("flattens skill-authored text so it cannot inject instruction lines", () => {
     const manifest = buildSkillLibraryManifestMarkdown({
       entries: [
diff --git a/packages/adapter-utils/src/skill-library-manifest.ts b/packages/adapter-utils/src/skill-library-manifest.ts
index 7350a5098..7b5bca09e 100644
--- a/packages/adapter-utils/src/skill-library-manifest.ts
+++ b/packages/adapter-utils/src/skill-library-manifest.ts
@@ -41,7 +41,10 @@ export function buildSkillLibraryManifestMarkdown(input: {
         const detail = entry.missingDetail ? sanitizeManifestText(entry.missingDetail, 200) : "";
         return `- ${key} — enabled but unavailable${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ""}`;
       }
-      return `- ${key} — ${enabled ? "enabled" : "installed, not enabled for you"}`;
+      if (!enabled) return `- ${key} — installed, not enabled for you`;
+      // The runtime only knows the mounted directory name, never the library key.
+      const runtimeName = sanitizeManifestText(entry.runtimeName, 200);
+      return `- ${key} — enabled; load it by its runtime name \`${runtimeName}\`, never by this key`;
     });
   return [
     "## Company skill library",
